},{"@type":"Service","name":"Homeowner Claim Appraisal","serviceType":"Insurance appraisal","description":"Homeowner claim appraisal in Maine for capes, colonials and farmhouses when the carrier’s estimate won’t cover the real cost of repairs.","provider":{"@id":"https://maineinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"areaServed":{"@type":"State","name":"Maine"},"url":"https://maineinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-work/homeowner-dispute-appraisal/","image":"https://maineinsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/snow-house.webp","@id":"https://maineinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-work/homeowner-dispute-appraisal/#service"},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is homeowner claim appraisal in Maine only for big losses?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, but the gap should be large enough to justify the appraiser’s fee and a share of the umpire. We help you run that math before you commit."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will my insurer cancel my policy if I demand appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Appraisal is a right written into the policy. If you are worried about nonrenewal, you can ask the Maine Bureau of Insurance about the rules that apply to your situation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can appraisal include contents as well as the house?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often yes, if the policy’s appraisal clause covers the whole amount of loss. Contents files need good inventories, receipts or photos to support value."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"My camp is on an island. Will the appraisal account for that?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Ferry or barge costs, crew travel time and limited working windows are real costs on island and remote properties, and we price them into the estimate."}}],"@id":"https://maineinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-work/homeowner-dispute-appraisal/#faq"}]}</script>
